  "body": "Lathe cross drills are no longer refused by the axial-hole check (issue #80).\n\n**What changed** (`crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`): `lathe_axial` is true only for a lathe Drill with no cross holes. A lathe cross drill already ran in radial verify mode; the shared verify tail's axial-hole check (it convicts any path without canned cycles) blocked every one with \"CD1: move 1 cuts past the finish surface\".\n\n**Checks a lathe cross drill still passes through** (none reads `lathe_axial`): #62 spindle law, #67 cross_spindle + lathe_reads, #77 raw-stock standoffs and rapid proof, #84 reach and holder, #79 radial rapids; #91's R-plane law is axial-only. Mixed axial + cross holes stay refused by name (split the op).\n\n**Pinned by** `lathe_cross_drill::a_clear_lathe_cross_drill_generates_with_no_blocking_warning_and_posts` (failed on main with `[Gouge { at: 1 }]`), plus guards `..._deeper_than_its_flute_is_still_refused_by_name`, `..._whose_bar_is_off_the_spindle_is_still_refused_by_name`, `an_axial_lathe_drill_where_the_bar_has_no_bore_is_still_convicted`; `drilling_cross_spindle` / `drilling_cross_stock` lathe cases now assert no blocking warnings.\n\n**Gates**: lathe_cross_drill 4, drilling_cross* , drilling_axial, drill_reach, drill_rplane, lathe_spindle_law, lathe_post, posting, conformance, golden_cl - green; clippy clean.\n\n**Gap found**: cross drilling never checks the hole against the finished part - #117.\n\nChangelog: fix(app): lathe cross drills are no longer refused by the axial-hole check (\"cuts past the finish surface\"); only axial lathe holes get that check\n\nFixes #80\n",
